# The digest of each version of the journal forwarder's package, plugins/journal-forwarder: one line per version, the
# version, a space, and the sha256 of the whole package as the runtime computes it — the number `jason plugin list` shows
# for an installed copy. It is the digest of the package a release publishes, which that release's runtime reports in
# `system.info`'s `released_plugins`; it is not the archive's checksum in `checksums.txt`. Each release's manifest carries
# the whole list as plugins.journal-forwarder.recorded, from which `jason update check` reads an installed copy's version
# by digest.
# The list starts with 1.0.0, the package v0.29.0 shipped in its tree, computed from that tag's tree: a copy made by
# hand from that release is read as 1.0.0 and updated. It holds every version the package has had, published or not,
# because every bump appends a line.
# A version is its content: any change to a file of the package is a new version, and a new version appends its line at
# the end, after the last edit to the package, since every edit changes the digest; once the version is bumped, the
# package's test prints the line to append. A line already here is never changed, and a line that changes or disappears
# in a diff is refused in review.
